 $ \left(v+u\right)^m-\left(v+u-1\right)^m =mv^{m-1}+ \dfrac{m-1}{2}v^{m-2}[u^2-(u-1)^2]+...$ 

Now let  $ u^2-\left(u-1\right)^2=0;u^3-(u-1)^3=0;...$ 

then we have that  $ \left(v+u\right)^m-\left(v+u-1\right)^m =m v^{n-1}$ 

Taking  $ v = 1,2,3, \ldots, n$  we have
 $ \begin{equation*}
\begin{alingned}
\left(u+1\right)^m-\left(u\right)^m &= m1^{m-1} 
\left(u+2\right)^m-\left(u+1\right)^m &= m2^{m-1} 
\vdots 
\left(u+n\right)^m-\left(u+n-1\right)^m &=mn^{m-1}
\end{alingned}$ 


Then we sum all of the equations and we obtain:

 $ \begin{equation*}
\begin{alingned}
(u+n)^m-u^m &= m(1^{m-1}+2^{m-1}+...+n^{m-1}) 
\dfrac{(u+n)^m-u^m}{m} &= 1^{m-1}+2^{m-1}+...+n^{m-1}
\end{alingned}$ 

where  $ u$  is a Bernoulli number

